{"title":"2009 Indonesia MO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a049abaf82e495dbbe3fd64f09590288a57e9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in\\{1,2,3,\\ldots,2009\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cdaab11884dd5aa4fc547b475a86851623b56c52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4n^6 + n^3 + 5\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />\nis divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For any real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> be the largest integer that is not more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Given a sequence of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b1681eacea3585aaf0086478b7a8218bff87fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,a_3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da9cfa8d9cd02104386314a76c5a7a06e939076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41ed37b1838ff25d878777dfd631e4d86fbcfbbf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\lfloor\\frac{a_1+1}{a_2}\\right\\rfloor=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{a_2+1}{a_3}\\right\\rfloor=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{a_3+1}{a_4}\\right\\rfloor=\\cdots\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"43\" />\nProve that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b30afd10e3ff652311e1f187a5b6f18fdef71be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left\\lfloor\\frac{a_n+1}{a_{n+1}}\\right\\rfloor\\leq1\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"43\" />\nholds for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For every triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/9575e1cb7b18dce01c064023128c9fd164ab5d9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D,E,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> be a point located on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2af80f0680f9428356964113ca9e3dd3577f324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,CA,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d4f683a69f4cb6598b26770cd2bf168e54fb83.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{AB}{AF}\\times DC+\\frac{AC}{AE}\\times DB=\\frac{AD}{AP}\\times BC\\]\" width=\"297\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In an island, there exist 7 towns and a railway system which connected some of the towns. Every railway segment connects 2 towns, and in every town there exists at least 3 railway segments that connects the town to another towns. Prove that there exists a route that visits 4 different towns once and go back to the original town. (Example: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448d778de3878fc264e8aa725afe89551571c9c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A-B-C-D-A$\" width=\"160\" height=\"13\" />)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a drawer, there are at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/85727a3ea4f5d7ba25bc591590b0e085bca557b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2009$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> balls, some of them are white, the rest are blue, which are randomly distributed. If two balls were taken at the same time, then the probability that the balls are both blue or both white is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc960c165b21ba43f7a90caa2893d40409d6944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Determine the maximum amount of white balls in the drawer, such that the probability statement is true?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the lowest possible values from the function\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c39bb8d14d8194e418854f16e7fc68e811996e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = x^{2008} - 2x^{2007} + 3x^{2006} - 4x^{2005} + 5x^{2004} - \\cdots - 2006x^3 + 2007x^2 - 2008x + 2009\\]\" width=\"623\" height=\"20\" />\nfor any real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A pair of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> is called good if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a0754474a34c9c889d6067784dc9c8dc9b1bc412.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m\\mid n^2 + n \\ \\text{and} \\ n\\mid m^2 + m\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />\nGiven 2 positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4349b8593e2a218b4efc7236e4a03a8fd30581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> which are relatively prime, prove that there exists a good pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/a/7ca10ffe3531cf1faf6222be7eac407c47bef878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/b/fab7b3c8f2111e4a83b930d4425c44f6e2ac5717.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\mid m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042ae3269503b1fb573e67637a433a883a6c6a46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\mid n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b1d363ea89ea929f3fe111de19a6de2b5177a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\nmid n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa05189bd74107ec4dd39dd0ebef393e9d12a4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\nmid m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given an acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The incircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> touches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2af80f0680f9428356964113ca9e3dd3577f324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC,CA,AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> respectively at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/9575e1cb7b18dce01c064023128c9fd164ab5d9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D,E,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. The angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/1/7b1ac662f7ddbbce489953c8b7693848239564aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> cuts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f0bd1bf44e9dd29cf5383c208c802b0dccb4920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> is one of the altitudes of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n(a) Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99dee7cbe9841dcd33578e2d5e134451fca20c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/2/4d21d821b4d355d89a283fb4770140d1497d26c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> are perpendicular with the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />.\n(b) Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769dfc28c2fe880d9d2d26bf3486c7c536043446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1KML$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO\">2009 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2008 Indonesia MO\">2008 Indonesia MO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2009 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2010 Indonesia MO\">2010 Indonesia MO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192958\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 304/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 986/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 82/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8665/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.690      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%   11.690      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16701:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192958 and revision id 97419. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}